  "query_preview": "..\nToday through Monday...\n\nBreezy winds will spread across portions of south-central Montana\ntoday, as the main axis of an upper trough continues to move \neastward. Gusts along and north of I-90/94 from Livingston to \nBaker are forecast to be in the 20 to 40 mph range, greatest along\nthe foothills west of Billings.\n\nHigh temperatures are forecast to be seasonable this week, in the\n60s and low 70sF. Easterly flow arrives on Wednesday with a weak \nwave. This looks to persist through the end of the week. This \npattern could allow cooler air to drop into the region from Canada\nas well. Light showers are possible in the east Wednesday night. \nModels are currently depicting an area of convergence bringing \nprecipitation from any upper wave Thursday afternoon into Friday \nmorning. Very little instability is shown by soundings, so showers\nlook to be the main course.\n\nAn additional trough swinging through the region is shown by \nensembles to end the week, this could bring additional \nprecipitation and cooler temperatures as well. Uncertainty remains\nhowever, so continue to monitor the forecast throughout the week.\n\nMatos",
